There’s a useful mechanism inside that, but the “whatever you want” part is where it breaks.

If you actually listen to a woman, respect what she tells you, follow through, notice her preferences, and stop trying to force outcomes, you often create more trust and openness. That can make her more willing to meet you halfway.

But that is responsiveness, not control.

The dangerous version is a covert contract: I did everything you asked, therefore you owe me the outcome I wanted. That usually poisons the very trust that made openness possible.

And women are not one behavioral system. A better rule is:

listen → understand → respond → build trust → state what you want clearly → let her choose → negotiate the overlap

Sometimes doing exactly what she says will get you closer to what you want because you finally addressed the thing blocking connection. Sometimes it won’t, because her desires are genuinely different from yours.

That distinction matters a lot in sex and marriage: influence is real; entitlement is not.